From 3fe3df7ace1b8e6555629ef3200ee3074b81261c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 18:36:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] feat: wire the proposal page's static UI text to
 next-intl
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extracts every hardcoded English string across the proposal page's
9 rendering components (ProposalHero, ProposalNarrative, CinematicGallery,
FeaturedExperience, ExperienceCard, IncludedExperiences,
ProposalEnhancements, FloatingPriceBar, ReservationSection, ShareButton)
into en.json under a new "proposal" namespace, replacing reads from
the old proposalConfig.ts static labels and inline hardcoded strings.

- formatPrice() now returns labelKey/valueKey instead of literal text,
  since it's a plain function without hook access — callers resolve
  the actual string via useTranslations("proposal").
- Guest-count sentence in ProposalHero ("N adults and M children") is
  now composed from singular/plural message keys instead of manual
  string interpolation, matching the pattern already used in the
  configurator.
- it.json picks these keys up automatically via the Lara auto-translate
  prebuild script on next build.

Not in scope here: enhancement.title/description/button text come
straight from the enhancements DB table and have no translation
pipeline at all yet (no enhancements_translations table exists) —
that's a new feature, not a fix, and needs a DB migration I can't run
from here.
